Routing logic: the car is stuck right now, which defaults to roadside_assistance. The tie-break sends it to needs_human only if the customer also reports that a repair we did caused it or demands a manager. Here the customer says the car has the same problem after a repair we did ("exact same thing," "resolved"). That is a repeat failure of our repair, not clearly a repair that caused a new failure, but it is close. The customer does not demand a manager or a person. They ask for a tow and a written explanation, which is something staff can provide but is not an insistence on a human.

The "same issue returned after our repair" case is best read as a repair-related failure, so I'm treating it as roadside_assistance with the repair_status as secondary. The escalation is safety because someone is stranded.

